export const SIGN_ON_CUSP: CuspText = {
  Aries: {
    "2": `Money is fuel rather than a cushion for you. You earn quickly, decide quickly and would rather chase a fresh income stream than nurse an old one, and your sense of worth rises when you can point to something you won by your own effort. The shadow is impulse: the purchase made just to feel alive, the bruised pride when savings dip. Sleep on big spends for one night, and let that courage build something that lasts.`,
    "3": `Conversation is a sport here. You say what you think before the sentence has fully formed, ask blunt questions and learn by diving in rather than reading the manual. Siblings, neighbours and classmates may know you as the one who starts the debate. The edge is impatience — interrupting, dismissing slower thinkers, arguing to win. Practise asking the second, curious question, and your directness becomes something people actively seek out.`,
    "4": `Home works as a base camp, a place to refuel between adventures rather than somewhere to sit still. You may rearrange the furniture on a whim, move more often than most, or come from a household full of strong opinions and lively clashes. Tempers can flare quickly behind closed doors. Give yourself one space that is unmistakably yours, and learn that rest and retreat are not the same thing as losing momentum.`,
    "5": `Play has to have a pulse. You flirt boldly, create in bursts of hot inspiration and love any hobby with a hint of competition or risk in it. Romance often begins with a chase, and you are rarely shy about making the first move. The shadow is boredom once the thrill settles, and projects abandoned halfway through. Choose one creative fire to tend past its first blaze, and see what it becomes.`,
    "6": `Routines bend to your energy, not the other way round. You work best with clear targets, quick wins and the freedom to tackle tasks in your own order, and you can clear a week's backlog in one fierce afternoon. Repetition makes you restless, and being micromanaged may make you bristle. Build short sprints into your day, celebrate a finished list, and save a little fire for the dull but necessary jobs.`,
    "7": `Partnerships wake you up. You are drawn to people who are direct, spirited and a little challenging, and the relationships that last tend to include honest friction and plenty of independence on both sides. Open rivals sharpen you rather than frighten you. The growth edge is noticing when you hand your own assertiveness to a partner, then resent how forceful they seem. Claim your own fire, and equality follows naturally.`,
    "8": `Intimacy needs honesty with nothing held back. You prefer to meet hard feelings head on, may move quickly into closeness, and handle shared money or joint decisions with a frank, let's-sort-it-now attitude. The shadow is rushing transformation — stirring up a crisis just to feel something shift. Trust that deep change can also unfold slowly. A candle lit for whatever you are ready to release can mark the turning point quietly.`,
    "9": `Belief is something you test by living it. You would rather book the ticket than read the guidebook, and your philosophy tends to be forged on the road, in a heated debate or through a course you signed up for on impulse. You can be fiercely sure of your truth, sometimes too sure. Leave room for the teacher who disagrees with you; convictions grow stronger, not weaker, for being challenged.`,
    "11": `Among friends you are the spark, the one who suggests the plan and gets everyone moving. You gravitate towards groups with a cause or a clear goal, and your hopes for the future tend to be bold and urgent. The shadow is clashing with other strong personalities, or leaving a circle the moment it slows down. Let others lead sometimes; shared dreams travel further when more than one person carries the torch.`,
    "12": `Your hidden life runs hot. Alone, you may replay arguments, rehearse brave speeches or feel restless energy with nowhere to go, and anger you never voiced can quietly pile up. Yet solitude can also be a place of fierce renewal. A brisk solo walk at dawn, a candle meditation or a journal written fast and unfiltered helps you hear your own courage before you need it out in the world.`,
  },
  Taurus: {
    "2": `Security is something you build slowly and keep carefully. You like money you can watch grow, objects that feel good in the hand, and a few beautiful things rather than many cheap ones. Your self-worth steadies when life has a reliable rhythm. The shadow is clinging — to possessions, habits or a job long outgrown — out of fear of loss. Let value circulate a little; generosity often feels richer than holding on.`,
    "3": `You think before you speak, and when you do speak people tend to listen. Learning sinks in through repetition, hands-on practice and an unhurried pace, and once you know something you know it for good. Your neighbourhood matters to you: the familiar café, the usual walk, the faces you nod to. Stubbornness is the edge. Try holding one opinion lightly each week, and notice what shifts.`,
    "4": `Home is a sanctuary, and you put real care into making it one. Soft textures, good food, a garden or even a windowsill of herbs help you feel rooted, and you may stay in one place longer than most people do. Family traditions can matter deeply. The risk is resisting needed change for the sake of comfort. Keep the roots, but let the rooms breathe and evolve as you do.`,
    "5": `Pleasure is your creative doorway. You romance through the senses — a shared meal, a slow evening, a handwritten note — and you create best with your hands, whether that means pottery, baking, music or gardening. You take your time before falling for someone and stay loyal once you have. The shadow is possessiveness, or settling so deep into comfort that play stops. Keep inviting surprise into what you love.`,
    "6": `Steady routines are where you shine. You like a predictable working day, tasks you can finish properly and tools of decent quality, and colleagues come to rely on your patience and follow-through. Rushed deadlines and sudden changes may unsettle you more than you admit. The growth edge is the rut. Refresh one habit each season, and let your daily work include something that genuinely pleases your senses.`,
    "7": `Partners need to feel safe, loyal and real to you. Grand gestures matter less than consistency: someone who turns up, keeps promises and enjoys simple pleasures with you. You may stay in partnerships, personal or professional, long after they stop growing, simply because they are familiar. Open rivals meet a calm, immovable wall. Notice where security has quietly become stagnation, and talk openly about what each of you values.`,
    "8": `Trust is earned slowly, and you guard your inner world until you feel truly safe. With shared finances you prefer clear, practical arrangements and may feel uneasy when resources are pooled or uncertain. Change can feel like the ground moving. Yet once you commit to a transformation, you see it through with remarkable steadiness. Let letting go be gradual and tangible — one drawer, one debt, one old story at a time.`,
    "9": `Wisdom has to be practical to earn a place in your life. You trust ideas that work in real kitchens and real relationships, and you may prefer slow travel, returning to beloved places or learning a craft over abstract theory. Clever arguments rarely move you; lived experience does. The edge is a closed door towards the unfamiliar. Taste a new culture through its food, and let curiosity widen your ground.`,
    "11": `Friendship, for you, is long and loyal. You may keep a small circle for decades, and you show up for friends with practical help rather than speeches. Your hopes tend to be concrete: a home you love, a business, a steady creative life. The shadow is resisting newcomers or holding grudges within groups. Open the door to one fresh connection a year; your loyalty is a gift worth sharing widely.`,
    "12": `In private you crave quiet comfort, and solitude often runs through the senses: music, cooking alone, a long soak, an afternoon among trees. Hidden worries tend to circle around security and whether there will be enough. Your spiritual life can be beautifully grounded — a smooth stone in your pocket, a garden tended like a prayer. The growth edge is letting comfort become avoidance. Rest deeply, then return refreshed.`,
  },
  Gemini: {
    "2": `Money tends to arrive through more than one channel, and you may enjoy juggling several skills or side projects at once. Your sense of worth is tied to your mind: being clever, informed and useful with words. You spend happily on books, gadgets, courses and anything that sparks conversation. The shadow is scattering resources across too many ideas. Track your spending like a story for a month, and the plot will reveal itself.`,
    "3": `This is home ground for a quick mind. You talk, text, read and question constantly, and you can pick up the basics of almost anything in an afternoon. Siblings and neighbours may be lively, chatty presences in your story. The edge is skimming — knowing a little about everything and staying with nothing. Choose one subject to go deep on, and your natural fluency turns into real expertise.`,
    "4": `Your home is full of chatter, books and comings and goings. You may have moved often, grown up around lively conversation, or feel most rooted when your space has room for ideas and visitors. Stillness at home can feel oddly uncomfortable. The shadow is never quite settling, or keeping family talk light to sidestep deeper feeling. Create one quiet corner where your busy mind is allowed to rest.`,
    "5": `Wit is your love language. You flirt through banter, messages and shared jokes, and you are drawn to people who keep you guessing. Creatively you thrive on variety — writing, word games, puzzles, quick sketches, anything playful and clever. The shadow is restlessness, keeping romance or projects on the surface so nothing feels too heavy. Let one story run long enough to surprise you with its depth.`,
    "6": `Variety keeps your working day alive. You handle several tasks at once, enjoy roles full of communication and lose interest fast in repetitive routines. You may reorganise your schedule constantly, trying every new app and system. The edge is nervous busyness: many things started, few finished. Break your day into short, varied blocks, complete one before beginning the next, and your adaptability becomes a genuine professional strength.`,
    "7": `Above all, a partner has to be good company in conversation. Mental connection, humour and shared curiosity hold your relationships together, and you value a partner who is flexible and sociable. Partnerships that fall silent or predictable lose their pull. Open rivals usually meet you in a war of words. The growth edge is staying committed through changing moods. Keep talking, especially when drifting would be easier.`,
    "8": `Intimacy begins in words for you. Honest conversations about desire, fear and money help you feel close, and you may be fascinated by the psychology of what lies beneath the surface. Shared resources work best when everything is discussed openly. The shadow is intellectualising feelings to avoid actually feeling them. Next time something stirs, name the emotion out loud before you analyse it; depth starts there.`,
    "9": `Your beliefs are a library still being written. You collect ideas from many traditions, love short trips and lively classes, and may change your mind as you learn more. Higher learning appeals most when it is varied and conversational. The edge is never committing to a worldview solid enough to hold you. Let one philosophy become a home rather than a hotel, while keeping your delightful curiosity.`,
    "11": `Your social life is wide and buzzing. You collect friends from every corner, introduce people who ought to know each other and thrive in groups built around ideas and shared interests. Your hopes shift as you discover new possibilities. The shadow is many acquaintances and few confidants. Choose a handful of people to know deeply; a wide web is strongest when a few of its threads are thick.`,
    "12": `Your private mind rarely goes quiet. Alone, thoughts can race and loop late into the night, and worries may hide inside the stories you tell yourself. Yet solitude is also where you write, dream in words and catch sudden flashes of intuition. Journalling before bed helps empty the chatter onto the page, and a simple repeated mantra gives your restless mind a single thread to follow.`,
  },
  Cancer: {
    "2": `Money is emotional for you, bound up with safety and caring for the people you love. You may save carefully, keep sentimental objects for years and feel most secure when the cupboards are full. Your self-worth can rise and fall with your moods. The shadow is spending to soothe or holding on out of fear. Build a cushion that feels nurturing, and remember your worth is never measured in reserves.`,
    "3": `You listen as much as you speak, and you remember how words made people feel. Learning sticks when it connects to emotion or personal stories, and you may keep close, protective ties with siblings or neighbours. Your tone shifts with your mood. The edge is taking passing comments personally or retreating into silence. Say gently what you feel; your emotional intelligence makes you a remarkably caring communicator.`,
    "4": `Home sits at the very heart of your life. You build nests, keep family rituals, cook for loved ones and feel the moods of the household deeply. Roots, ancestry and memory carry real emotional weight. The shadow is clinging to the past or repeating old family patterns without question. Honour your lineage with a small shelf of photographs or keepsakes, and choose consciously which traditions you carry forward.`,
    "5": `You love with tenderness and creative feeling. Romance tends to grow out of emotional safety — you want to feel cared for before you open up fully. Creativity flows from memory and mood: poetry, home cooking, photography, songs about belonging. The shadow is moodiness, or holding back for fear of rejection. Let play be safe and silly; when you feel held, your heart is wonderfully generous.`,
    "6": `Your working day runs on feeling. You do your best work in a supportive environment where people look out for each other, and you often become the colleague who notices when someone is struggling. Routines that feel nurturing help you stay steady. The edge is carrying work worries home or over-caring for everyone else. Set gentle boundaries, and make your daily rhythm as kind to you as you are to others.`,
    "7": `What you want most in a partner is someone who feels like home. Emotional security, loyalty and tenderness matter more than status, and you may find yourself caring for partners or attracting people who want to care for you. Open rivalry stings more than you show. The growth edge is slipping into parent-like roles in adult relationships. Share your needs openly, so both of you can nurture and be nurtured.`,
    "8": `Closeness is a deep need, and you open up slowly but completely once trust has formed. Shared resources feel emotional, tied to family, care and protection. You may hold onto old hurts longer than you intend. The shadow is clinging when change is calling. Transformation comes through feeling everything fully, then gently releasing it; writing down what you are ready to let go of at the full moon can help close a chapter.`,
    "9": `Your philosophy grows from your roots. Family traditions, ancestral stories and emotional experience shape what you believe, and travel feels best when it carries a sense of homecoming or belonging. You may learn most from teachers who feel nurturing. The edge is holding onto beliefs absorbed in childhood without ever questioning them. Visit somewhere your family has never been, and let new soil nourish the views you already hold.`,
    "11": `Friends become family to you. You nurture your circle, remember birthdays and create a feeling of home in any group you join. Your hopes often centre on belonging, community and emotional security. The shadow is feeling hurt when friends do not return your care in kind, or clinging to circles you have outgrown. Let friendships breathe and change naturally; your warmth always finds its people.`,
    "12": `Alone, you feel everything — the past, other people's moods, memories you thought were finished. Solitude restores you, but only when you protect it from everyone else's emotional weather. Your spiritual life is often lunar and intuitive, tied to water and the moon's phases. The shadow is retreating into old hurts. A quiet new moon ritual, or simply sitting by water, can help you clear and begin again.`,
  },
  Leo: {
    "2": `You like money that lets you live generously. You may spend on beauty, celebrations and gifts that delight the people you love, and your self-worth thrives when your talents are recognised. Earning through creativity, performance or leadership can feel natural. The shadow is spending to impress, or tying your value to applause. Keep a private treasury of pride that does not depend on anyone else's admiration.`,
    "3": `Warmth, drama and conviction colour the way you speak. Stories, performance and a touch of theatre make you memorable, and you learn best when a subject genuinely excites you. Among siblings or classmates you may have been the storyteller or the ringleader. The edge is dominating conversation or needing to be right. Invite others to share their stories too; your charisma shines brighter when it lights other people up.`,
    "4": `Whatever its size, home is your stage and your palace. You like a warm, colourful space where people gather and feel welcome, and you may feel fiercely proud of your family or roots. The shadow is wanting home life to reflect well on you, or household dramas that play out for attention. Create a home that feels joyful even when nobody is watching, and let warmth flow both ways.`,
    "5": `Here your heart is fully at home. You love grandly, flirt with charm and create with real confidence, whether through acting, painting, styling or hosting a memorable evening. Romance needs devotion, admiration and a little theatre. The shadow is needing constant applause, or sulking when you feel overlooked. Keep creating for the joy of it rather than only for the audience, and your playful heart stays generous and bright.`,
    "6": `Everyday work gets your warmth and your pride. You like to be appreciated for your effort, and you may naturally take charge of projects or brighten the office with humour. Dull routines frustrate you unless they lead somewhere meaningful. The edge is needing praise to stay motivated. Find personal pride in quiet tasks done beautifully; your consistency is a kind of radiance, even when no one comments on it.`,
    "7": `You admire partners who are confident, warm and a little dazzling. Loyalty, generosity and shared celebration matter, and you may secretly hope relationships will feel like a great romance. Open rivals bring out your pride. The growth edge is projecting your own radiance onto a partner and then feeling eclipsed by them. Let both of you shine, and the partnership becomes a celebration rather than a competition.`,
    "8": `In intimacy you give your whole heart and expect loyalty in return. Shared resources may be handled generously, though pride can make it hard to ask for help when you need it. Deep change can feel like a threat to your sense of self, yet you often come through it stronger and brighter. The shadow is guarding vulnerability behind a proud face. Let someone see you uncrowned; closeness deepens there.`,
    "9": `Bold, warm and heartfelt — that is how your beliefs tend to look. You are drawn to philosophies that celebrate creativity and self-expression, and you may love travel that feels like a grand adventure worth retelling. Teaching or sharing what you know comes naturally. The edge is preaching rather than inspiring. Stay a student even while you lead, and your enthusiasm will open doors for people far beyond your circle.`,
    "11": `In groups you are a natural host and a loyal friend. You bring warmth, ideas and a sense of occasion to any gathering, and your hopes tend to be big, creative and heartfelt. The shadow is wanting to be the centre of every circle, or feeling slighted when friends forget to include you. Celebrate other people's successes as loudly as your own, and your friendships turn golden.`,
    "12": `Privately, your heart longs to be seen and sometimes wonders whether it really is. Hidden pride, or a quiet fear of being ordinary, can drain you when you are alone. Yet solitude can become wonderfully creative: writing, painting or singing for no audience at all. The growth edge is learning that your light does not need witnesses to be real. A single candle lit just for you can be your reminder.`,
  },
  Virgo: {
    "2": `Money is managed with care and an eye for detail. You track spending, compare prices and take quiet pride in getting real value, and your self-worth grows when you feel useful and competent. Skill, precision and practical services can be natural ways for you to earn. The shadow is anxious budgeting or feeling never quite good enough. Plan sensibly, then step back; your careful habits deserve your trust, and small treats are allowed.`,
    "3": `Your mind is precise, observant and analytical. You learn through detail, ask exact questions and notice the errors others miss, and you may be the sibling or neighbour people come to for practical advice. Writing, editing and research can come naturally. The edge is overthinking, or criticism dressed up as helpfulness. Lead with appreciation before correction, and your sharp mind becomes a source of genuine support.`,
    "4": `Order brings you peace at home. You like a clean, functional, well-organised space, and you may express love through practical care for the people you live with. Your roots might include a household of routines, duties or quiet responsibility. The shadow is never relaxing at home because something always needs fixing. Leave one corner beautifully imperfect, and let home be a place of rest as well as order.`,
    "5": `Care and craftsmanship shape your approach to romance and creativity. You show love by noticing small details and doing thoughtful things, and your creative work is often made with precision — knitting, illustration, writing, baking from a well-thumbed recipe. The shadow is perfectionism that stifles play, or hesitating to show your feelings. Give yourself permission to make messy things purely for fun, and let love be imperfect and delightful.`,
    "6": `Daily work is where your talents feel most at home. You thrive on routines, systems and doing a job properly, and colleagues come to rely on your eye for detail and your quiet reliability. Roles involving service or problem-solving can suit you beautifully. The edge is overwork and worry. Set clear limits on your day, and remember that being useful is only one of the many sources of your value.`,
    "7": `Thoughtful, competent, helpful partners appeal to you most. Relationships thrive on practical care, shared tasks and clear communication, and you notice small things that could be adjusted or improved. Open rivals face your sharp analysis. The growth edge is critique — of yourself or of the person beside you. Practise daily appreciation out loud, and let love be less about improvement and more about acceptance.`,
    "8": `You approach intimacy carefully, analysing feelings before you let yourself trust them. Shared money and joint responsibilities are handled with order, and you may be the one who quietly sorts the paperwork everyone else avoids. Deep transformation can feel unsettling until you understand it. The shadow is worrying instead of feeling. Write down what you fear and what you need; clarity can open the door to closeness.`,
    "9": `Your beliefs are practical and carefully researched. You trust ideas that are useful and well reasoned, and you may love mastering a skill or studying one subject thoroughly. Travel often involves meticulous planning and real attention to local detail. The edge is losing the bigger picture among the small print. Leave space for wonder on every journey, and let your faith in life grow beyond what can be checked.`,
    "11": `You are the friend who helps. You may organise group events, offer practical advice and show care through quiet acts of service, and your hopes often involve making things better in tangible ways. The shadow is feeling unappreciated, or criticising the group's chaos from the sidelines. Let friends support you in return. A small, steady circle of thoughtful people may suit you better than a crowd.`,
    "12": `In private your mind keeps working, sorting and evaluating, and hidden worries about getting things right can cloud your solitude. Yet retreat can also hold a quiet, devoted spiritual practice — a simple morning ritual, a bundle of dried herbs, ten minutes of stillness. The shadow is self-criticism behind closed doors. Treat yourself, especially when alone, with the same gentle care you so readily give everyone else.`,
  },
  Libra: {
    "2": `Beauty and balance shape how you earn and spend. You are drawn to lovely things — good clothes, art, a well-set table — and may earn through partnership, design or diplomacy. Your self-worth can lean on other people's approval or on keeping the peace. The shadow is indecision over money, or overspending on appearances. Decide what truly matters to you, and let your sense of value be entirely your own.`,
    "3": `Words, for you, are bridges. You speak tactfully, see every side of an argument and can calm a heated room with the right phrase. Learning goes best in pairs or groups where ideas bounce back and forth. Siblings and neighbours may see you as the peacemaker. The edge is saying what people want to hear rather than what you actually think. Let honesty and kindness sit side by side.`,
    "4": `Harmony, beauty and calm are what you need from home. You may decorate with real care, avoid conflict in the household and feel unsettled by clutter or tension in the air. Family life might have taught you to keep the peace at almost any cost. The shadow is swallowing your feelings to avoid disagreement. Fill your space with soft light and lovely things, and let honest conversations keep the atmosphere clear.`,
    "5": `Romance feels like an art form to you. You love courtship, elegance and shared beauty, and your creativity flows through design, music, dance or anything harmonious. You may be drawn to people who are graceful and charming. The shadow is falling for an ideal, or avoiding conflict in love until it festers. Enjoy the dance, but let real feelings — even awkward ones — have their place on the floor.`,
    "6": `Pleasant, cooperative surroundings bring out your best work. Teamwork, fairness and a well-designed workspace help you thrive, and you may naturally mediate between colleagues who clash. Harsh routines or constant conflict drain your motivation quickly. The edge is putting off unpleasant tasks, or overcommitting to keep everyone happy. Set fair boundaries for yourself, and let each working day include something beautiful, however small.`,
    "7": `Partnership is central to your life, and you often see yourself most clearly through the people you love or work with. You value fairness, courtesy and grace, and you may idealise relationships or keep score of who gives what. Open rivals are met with diplomacy. The shadow is losing yourself in the other person. Keep your own voice in every partnership, and true balance becomes possible.`,
    "8": `Even in the deepest places, you seek balance. Intimacy grows through fairness, mutual respect and a sense of beauty, and you may handle shared resources by insisting on equal terms. Intense emotions can feel unsettling, and you might sidestep them to keep things pleasant. The shadow is avoiding necessary confrontation. Transformation comes when difficult truths are spoken kindly. A piece of rose quartz kept close can remind you that love includes depth.`,
    "9": `Fairness, beauty and the search for harmony shape your beliefs. You may love art, philosophy or travel to beautiful places, and you learn especially well alongside a study partner. You can see every perspective, sometimes too well. The edge is indecision about what you truly believe. Let yourself take a stand now and then, and your openness becomes wisdom rather than endless weighing.`,
    "11": `You are a gracious friend and a natural connector. Groups feel better with you in them, and your hopes often involve partnership, beauty and fairness in the wider world. Disagreements among friends may unsettle you. The shadow is losing your own opinions to keep the peace. Speak up within your circle, and trust that honest friendships survive disagreement — they usually grow stronger for it.`,
    "12": `In private you long for peace, and hidden tension can build when relationships feel out of balance. Solitude is restful when it includes beauty — music, art, a quiet garden, a softly lit room. You may find spiritual meaning through gentle ritual, meditative movement or simply creating harmony around you. The shadow is hiding conflict until it surfaces. Let solitude be where you hear your own wishes, not just everyone else's.`,
  },
  Scorpio: {
    "2": `Money carries power and privacy for you. You may keep your finances to yourself, research every major purchase and feel safest when you have resources others do not know about. Your self-worth is tied to resilience — knowing you can rebuild from almost nothing. The shadow is control, or all-or-nothing swings between strict saving and intense spending. Let money be a tool rather than a fortress, and share a little more freely.`,
    "3": `You speak carefully and listen for what is not being said. Conversations tend to go deep fast, and you learn best through research, investigation and getting to the bottom of things. Siblings or neighbours may have shared intense bonds or secrets with you. The edge is cutting words when you feel threatened, or keeping too much hidden. Share what you discover, and your perception becomes real insight.`,
    "4": `Home is a private den, and you protect it fiercely. You need a space where you can be completely yourself, away from prying eyes, and your family story may contain strong emotions, secrets or transformations. The shadow is carrying old intensity into the present. Clear your space regularly — open the windows, burn a little sage or simply rearrange — and let home renew as you do.`,
    "5": `You love deeply and play intensely. Romance is magnetic, passionate and rarely casual, and your creativity draws on the hidden, the dark and the transformative — poetry, photography, mystery, ritual. The shadow is jealousy, or testing people to see if they will stay. Let play be lighter now and then, and allow joy without needing it to be profound every time.`,
    "6": `Focus and determination define your working day. You can dig into a task with remarkable depth, solve problems others give up on and keep going long after colleagues have left. You may prefer to work alone or in roles that require discretion. The edge is obsession, or power struggles at work. Pace yourself, let some tasks be good enough, and trust colleagues with more of your plans.`,
    "7": `Partnership is never shallow for you. You seek depth, loyalty and emotional honesty, and you may attract partners who are intense, private or transformative. Open rivals are watched carefully. The growth edge is control — trying to hold a relationship so tightly it cannot breathe. Trust grows through openness, so share your own vulnerability first, and the bond becomes truly unbreakable.`,
    "8": `This is deep water, and you swim in it naturally. Intimacy, shared resources and transformation are areas you take seriously, and you may sense what others hide. You can handle intensity that would overwhelm many people. The shadow is secrecy or using knowledge as power. Let transformation be a shared journey, and your capacity for depth becomes a profound gift to those you trust.`,
    "9": `Your beliefs must be tested in the fire. You are drawn to philosophies that probe the mysteries of life, the hidden and the taboo, and travel may feel like a quest for transformation. You may study psychology, occult traditions or anything with depth. The edge is fanaticism or suspicion of other views. Stay curious rather than certain, and your search becomes truly wise.`,
    "11": `Friendship, for you, is a sacred trust. You may have few friends but extremely deep bonds, and you are fiercely loyal to your inner circle. Your hopes are often intense and transformative. The shadow is suspicion of groups or cutting people off entirely when hurt. Let friendships survive a disagreement, and trust grows deeper with each storm weathered.`,
    "12": `Your inner world is rich, intense and often hidden. Alone, you may confront old fears, secrets or feelings you rarely share, and solitude can be powerfully transformative. Your spiritual life may draw on shadow work, dreams or deep ritual. The shadow is getting lost in dark feelings. Balance inner exploration with light — a candle, a friend, a walk — and your hidden depth becomes a source of power.`,
  },
  Sagittarius: {
    "2": `Optimism shapes your relationship with money. You trust that resources will come, spend generously on travel, learning and experiences, and may earn through teaching, publishing or anything that broadens horizons. Your self-worth rests on freedom and meaning. The shadow is overspending or assuming luck will cover the gap. Keep your generous spirit, but give your adventures a budget so that freedom stays sustainable.`,
    "3": `Conversation is an adventure for you. You love big ideas, lively debate and stories from far away, and you may learn best through travel, discussion or wide reading. Siblings or neighbours may share your love of exploration or argument. The edge is bluntness or preaching. Ask questions as eagerly as you share answers, and your enthusiasm becomes truly infectious.`,
    "4": `Home is wherever you can roam freely. You may have moved a lot, lived in different cultures or need space to come and go as you please. Family life may have been philosophical, adventurous or a little chaotic. The shadow is restlessness that never lets you settle. Create a home with maps, books and windows open to the horizon, and let rootedness and freedom coexist.`,
    "5": `Fun means adventure for you. You flirt with humour, honesty and enthusiasm, and you are drawn to people who expand your world. Creativity flows when it involves exploration, storytelling or the outdoors. The shadow is avoiding commitment or treating romance like a holiday. Let joy be expansive, but stay long enough to discover how deep a love or project can go.`,
    "6": `Freedom matters in your daily work. You prefer flexible schedules, varied tasks and work with a sense of purpose, and you may thrive in roles involving teaching, travel or big-picture thinking. Detailed routines can feel confining. The edge is overpromising and underdelivering. Break big visions into small daily steps, and let your optimism inspire consistent action.`,
    "7": `You seek partners who are adventurous, honest and open-minded. Relationships thrive on shared exploration, humour and plenty of space, and you may be drawn to people from different backgrounds or cultures. Open rivals meet your frankness. The growth edge is commitment without feeling trapped. Talk openly about freedom, and your partnership can become a lifelong adventure rather than a cage.`,
    "8": `You approach intimacy and shared resources with openness and optimism. You may be generous with joint finances, see transformation as a chance for growth, and seek meaning in deep experiences. The shadow is avoiding heavy feelings by escaping into the next adventure. Stay present with what is hard; your faith that something good emerges from change is a gift when you let it work slowly.`,
    "9": `This is home ground for your seeking spirit. Travel, philosophy and higher learning feel like breathing, and you may collect teachers, books and passport stamps with delight. Your beliefs are expansive and generous. The edge is dogmatism or restless searching without ever settling. Let wisdom be something you live day to day, not just a destination always just beyond the horizon.`,
    "11": `Friendship, for you, is a journey shared. You collect friends from many places and walks of life, and groups feel alive when you bring your humour and big ideas. Your hopes are often bold, idealistic and wide-reaching. The shadow is unreliability or moving on too fast. Invest in the friends who have travelled with you, and your circle becomes a lifelong caravan.`,
    "12": `In private you search for meaning and may feel restless when life seems small. Solitude restores you best when it involves nature, open space or spiritual study. Hidden hopes and faith in something greater sustain you. The shadow is escaping into the next big idea to avoid inner work. Sit still sometimes; the deepest journey is the one inward.`,
  },
  Capricorn: {
    "2": `Money is a long-term project for you. You save steadily, plan ahead and take quiet pride in security you built through your own effort, and your self-worth often climbs alongside your achievements. Even when you can afford a treat, you may hesitate. The shadow is equating your value with your balance or your job title. Build wisely, but let yourself enjoy some of what you have earned along the way.`,
    "3": `Words carry weight for you, so you choose them carefully. You prefer conversations that are useful, structured and to the point, and learning comes through discipline, patient practice and a good teacher. Siblings or neighbours may have expected maturity from you early on. The edge is sounding cold, or holding back an opinion until it feels perfect. Let warmth soften your phrasing; your quiet authority becomes deeply trusted.`,
    "4": `Home is a foundation you build stone by stone. You may have taken on responsibility early in family life, and you tend to value tradition, structure and a household that runs well. Roots can feel serious or demanding, and you might be the one relatives lean on. The shadow is putting duty ahead of comfort. Create small rituals of rest at home, and let your space feel warm as well as secure.`,
    "5": `Patience and seriousness shape the way you play and love. Romance may develop slowly, built on respect and shared goals, and your creative work is often disciplined and built to last — a long novel, a craft honed over years, a garden planned in seasons. The shadow is treating fun like another task, or holding back joy until you feel you have earned it. Pleasure does not need a justification; let some in now.`,
    "6": `Discipline and responsibility run through your working day. You are reliable, organised and quietly ambitious, and colleagues soon learn that what you promise gets done. You may take on more than your share without complaint. The edge is grinding on without pause and calling it virtue. Build regular breaks into your schedule, notice what you have already achieved, and remember that steady, sustainable effort outlasts heroic marathons every time.`,
    "7": `Reliable, mature and committed partners appeal to you. Relationships tend to grow slowly and are built to last, and you may value someone who respects your ambitions and has plans of their own. Open rivals meet your strategic patience; you rarely rush a confrontation. The growth edge is treating partnership like a contract rather than a living bond. Let tenderness and spontaneity into the structure, and love deepens with time.`,
    "8": `Caution and responsibility guide you in the deepest areas of life. You may manage joint finances carefully, read the small print others skip and need real time before trusting someone fully. Transformation feels like serious work, and you rise to it with patience and grit. The shadow is emotional control, or fear of looking vulnerable. Let yourself be held sometimes; true strength includes the ability to soften.`,
    "9": `Experience and tradition ground your beliefs. You trust wisdom that has stood the test of time, and you may pursue higher learning with real discipline, perhaps returning to study later in life. Travel often has a purpose — a course, a project, a place with history. The edge is rigidity, dismissing ideas that lack a track record. Let new philosophies earn your respect gradually, and your wisdom grows richer with age.`,
    "11": `Friendships form slowly for you and often last a lifetime. You may keep a small circle of reliable people, and you tend to value groups with clear purpose, structure or shared ambition. Your hopes are practical and long-term, mapped out years ahead. The shadow is treating friendship as networking, or keeping your warmth in reserve. Let friends see your dry, playful side, and your loyal heart will be well loved.`,
    "12": `Privately you may carry worries about responsibility, falling short or not doing enough, and solitude can slip into planning rather than rest. Yet your spiritual life can be beautifully structured: a daily practice, an old tradition kept faithfully, a quiet hour that belongs to you alone. The shadow is secret self-pressure. Allow solitude to be soft. Rest, for you, can become a sacred duty rather than a reward.`,
  },
  Aquarius: {
    "2": `Money, for you, is mostly a tool for freedom. You may earn in unusual ways — through technology, community projects or ideas that are slightly ahead of their time — and your self-worth rests on independence and originality. Your spending habits can surprise even you. The shadow is shrugging off material needs until they become urgent. Set up simple, automatic systems that protect your freedom, and let your values steer your money.`,
    "3": `Original thinking is your signature. Ideas excite you, and you may be drawn to unusual subjects, new technology or debates about where the world is heading. Siblings or neighbours may have found you quirky or a step ahead. You often learn best by teaching yourself. The edge is stubbornness disguised as logic. Listen with genuine curiosity, and your inventive mind becomes a bridge others are glad to cross.`,
    "4": `Freedom and individuality matter most to you at home. You may come from an unconventional family, live in shared or unusual homes, or simply need room to be your own person under your own roof. Roots can feel complicated, something you redefine rather than simply receive. The shadow is keeping family at arm's length. Make home a laboratory of self-expression, and let warmth sit comfortably alongside your independence.`,
    "5": `Romance and creativity both take unexpected turns with you. You flirt through ideas, banter and friendship first, and your creative work may be experimental, digital or deliberately unconventional. Freedom in love is not negotiable. The shadow is emotional distance, staying clever when feelings would serve you better. Let your heart be as adventurous as your mind, and discover that intimacy and independence can grow together.`,
    "6": `Innovation and flexibility keep your daily work alive. Rigid routines frustrate you, and you may thrive in technology, team projects or roles with a social purpose. You are often the person who suggests a better system no one had considered. The edge is rebelling against structure that is actually useful. Design your own routines rather than rejecting routine altogether, and your originality will improve the way everything gets done.`,
    "7": `Partners need to be independent, original and open-minded to hold your interest. Friendship is the foundation of your relationships, and you need space to remain fully yourself within them. Unusual arrangements may suit you better than conventional scripts. Open rivals meet your cool, detached logic. The growth edge is emotional availability. Share feelings as readily as ideas, and partnership becomes both free and close.`,
    "8": `Curiosity and independence colour your approach to intimacy. You may handle shared resources in unconventional ways — separate accounts, clear agreements, nothing assumed — and transformation often arrives through a sudden flash of insight rather than slow change. The shadow is detaching from intense feelings by turning them into theories. Let yourself be moved, not merely interested. Emotional depth can become your most exciting new frontier.`,
    "9": `Progressive and independent, your beliefs are your own. You are drawn to new ideas, future-facing philosophies and travel that genuinely opens your mind, and you may question every tradition you are handed. Learning through online communities or self-directed study can suit you well. The edge is dismissing old wisdom simply because it is old. Blend innovation with respect for the past, and your vision becomes powerful.`,
    "11": `This is home ground for your community spirit. Friends, networks and causes give your life meaning, and you are drawn to people who share your vision of a fairer, freer future. Your hopes are idealistic and forward-looking. The shadow is caring about humanity in general while overlooking the friend in front of you. Make time for one-to-one connection, and your circle grows warm as well as wide.`,
    "12": `Privately you may feel like an outsider, even in a crowded room, and you might hide feelings that seem too ordinary for your independent image. Solitude lets you explore unusual ideas, intuitive flashes and spiritual paths of your own design. The shadow is isolation, or cutting off from feeling altogether. Let your inner world include warmth and compassion for yourself, and your hidden originality flourishes.`,
  },
  Pisces: {
    "2": `Money flows like water for you — sometimes in, sometimes out, rarely in a straight line. You may earn through creativity, care or intuition, and your self-worth is linked to compassion and imagination rather than possessions. You give generously, sometimes more than you can spare. The shadow is vagueness about what you have and owe. Build gentle, simple structures around your finances, and let your generosity become sustainable.`,
    "3": `Your mind moves in images, feelings and stories. You often sense what someone means before they finish speaking, and you may learn best through art, music, metaphor or full immersion rather than dry facts. Siblings or neighbours may experience you as gentle and dreamy. The edge is drifting off or avoiding difficult conversations. Ground your insights in clear, simple words, and your soft voice becomes truly reassuring.`,
    "4": `Home is a dreamy refuge, the place where you recharge after absorbing the world all day. You may need a peaceful, artistic space with music and soft light, and family life may have felt emotional, fluid or hard to define. The shadow is hiding away at home, or blurring boundaries with relatives. Keep a bowl of water or a sea-smoothed shell somewhere you can see it, and keep boundaries kind but clear.`,
    "5": `Romance, for you, is poetic and wholehearted. You fall for the story as much as the person, love with deep imagination and may create through music, dance, painting or writing that draws on dreams. Play can feel like slipping into another world. The shadow is idealising someone until reality disappoints. Enjoy the magic fully, but let love be real and human, flaws and all.`,
    "6": `Daily work needs meaning and compassion to hold your interest. You may thrive in creative or caring roles, and you often sense colleagues' moods before anyone says a word. Rigid routines can feel draining, while flexible rhythms help you flow. The edge is disorganisation, or quietly sacrificing your own needs to help everyone else. Build gentle structure into your day, and let intuition guide which tasks come first.`,
    "7": `Compassionate, artistic and spiritually minded partners draw you in. Relationships can feel like soul connections, and you may give a great deal of yourself to the people you love. Open rivals are often met with avoidance rather than confrontation. The growth edge is idealising partners or trying to rescue them. See people as they truly are, ask for what you need, and love becomes real rather than dreamed.`,
    "8": `Intimacy feels spiritual and boundless to you. You may merge emotionally with the people you love, sense their hidden feelings and let shared resources become blurred without noticing. Transformation tends to come through surrender rather than force. The shadow is losing yourself entirely in another person. Keep clear boundaries while still allowing depth; a short ritual of returning to yourself after closeness can help.`,
    "9": `Mystical and compassionate, your beliefs are shaped more by feeling than by doctrine. You may be drawn to spiritual traditions, sacred art, music or journeys that feel like pilgrimages, especially to the sea. You learn through inspiration and imagination. The edge is accepting ideas without question because they feel beautiful. Ground your faith in discernment, and your wide spiritual vision becomes truly wise.`,
    "11": `Friends can feel like soul family to you. You are drawn to compassionate groups, creative collectives and idealistic causes, and you often sense what your friends need before they ask. Your hopes may be dreamy and generous rather than precisely planned. The shadow is being taken advantage of, or losing your own wishes in the group's. Choose your circle with care, and let your kindness flow both ways.`,
    "12": `Here your soul feels at home. Solitude, dreams and spirituality nourish you deeply, and you may need regular time alone simply to sort your own feelings from everyone else's. Your intuition can be remarkably strong. The shadow is escapism — drifting away when life feels too sharp. Ground your spiritual life in a simple daily practice, perhaps a dream journal by the bed, and let your inner sea become a source of guidance.`,
  },
};
